    "alert_id": "ALERT_002",
    "title": "Low-level viremia on DTG-based regimen",
    "message": "Guidelines note that viral load >200 copies/mL is associated with risk of transmission and treatment failure, and that low-level viremia should be monitored. The patient's viral load was 40 copies/mL 113 days before this visit, which is detectable but below the suppression threshold. While on a DTG-based regimen (TLD), this low-level viremia warrants enhanced adherence counseling and repeat viral load testing to confirm whether suppression is achieved or viremia is progressing.",
    "issue_type": "guideline_deviation",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Repeat viral load testing and provide enhanced adherence counseling; evaluate for potential treatment failure if viremia persists or increases.",
